[   22.635] What went wrong
[   22.636] Immucore checks the OS image against the sha256 recorded for it
[   22.636] before it mounts it, and the check did not pass.
[   22.636] 
[   22.637]   Problem:
[   22.637]     the check ran out of time
[   22.638]   Image:
[   22.638]     /sysroot/run/initramfs/cos-state/cOS/active.img
[   22.639]   Expected sha256 (stored in active.img.sha256):
[   22.639]     815a1742f6fb57754bd13bad0a1576fada27589f941b0c3397a90cafced92742
[   22.639]   Actual sha256 (computed from the image just now):
[   22.640]     (not available)
[   22.640] 
[   22.641]   Hashing stopped after 5.04s (529530880 bytes read) because image-checksum.verify-timeout
[   22.643]   is 5s, so the image was not verified. require is on, so it counts as a failure.
[   22.643] 
[   22.643]   Action: fail (from kernel cmdline)
[   22.643]   A missing or stale checksum is a problem too: require is on
[   22.643]   (from kernel cmdline)
[   22.643] 
[   22.646] How to fix
[   22.646]   - Reboot and pick the passive or recovery entry in the boot menu.
[   22.646]     Then repair the image with kairos-agent upgrade or reset.
[   22.646]   - To boot this image anyway, edit the boot entry (press e) and add
[   22.646]     image-checksum.verify=warn to the kernel line.
[   22.658]   - A disk that corrupts images can corrupt more: check its health.
[   22.658] 
[   22.658] Where to look
[   22.658]   journalctl -b -u immucore
[   22.658]   /run/immucore/
